<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="git-addon-review-stage-commit">
  <title>Review, Stage, and Commit Changes</title>
  <shortdesc>Turn your edits into a commit: review what changed, stage the changes you want, and
    commit them to your local repository.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>staging changes</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>commits</indexterm></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <taskbody>
    <context>
      <p>You do all of this in the
        <uicontrol conref="lib/git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs-view"/> view.
        Modified files appear in the
        <uicontrol conref="lib/git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs-unstaged-files"/>
        area; staging moves the ones you choose into the
        <uicontrol conref="lib/git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs-staged-files"/>
        area, ready to commit.</p>
    </context>
    <steps>
      <step>
        <cmd>Review your changes in the
          <uicontrol conref="lib/git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs-unstaged-files"/>
          area.</cmd>
        <info>
          <p>Double-click a file to open it in the compare editor and see exactly what changed. See
              <xref href="git-addon-compare-changes.dita"/>.</p>
        </info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Stage the changes you want to commit.</cmd>
        <info>
          <p>Select files and use
              <uicontrol conref="lib/git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs-stage-selected"/>,
            or use
              <uicontrol conref="lib/git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs-stage-all"/>.
            To move a file back, use
              <uicontrol conref="lib/git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs-unstage-selected"/>
            or
              <uicontrol conref="lib/git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs-unstage-all"/>.</p>
        </info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Enter a message in the
          <uicontrol conref="lib/git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs-commit-message"/>
          area that describes the staged changes.</cmd>
        <info>
          <p>You can generate, reuse, or amend the message with the commit-area options. See
              <xref href="git-addon-commit-messages-with-ai.dita"/>.</p>
        </info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Select <uicontrol conref="lib/git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs-commit"/>.</cmd>
      </step>
    </steps>
    <result>
      <p>The Git Client records the staged changes as a commit in your local repository.
        <xref href="git-addon-push-commits.dita">Push</xref> when you're ready to share them.</p>
    </result>
  </taskbody>
</task>
